Cairo 1.16.0 port profile for BlockOS:

Required for GNOME/X11 target:
  - keep image backend
  - keep xlib/xcb backend when the BlockOS X11 client ABI is available
  - keep fontconfig/freetype integration for the later Pango stack

Disable unrelated host backends (Quartz, Win32, OS2, BeOS, DirectFB, Qt,
OpenGL/GLX unless a matching BlockOS renderer exists). Disable Cairo tests and
documentation in the cross build.

If BlockOS X11 is not yet ABI-complete, build image-only Cairo first; enabling
xlib/xcb before the X11 client library is available will not produce a usable
GNOME stack.
*** END PATCH SPEC ***
